    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d219">

                <pb facs="0218" n="206" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg206"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.24/312: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dreyfus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-12-04T19:00:00+03:25">December 4, 1942—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 5—3 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>419. Food declaration was signed this afternoon by Foreign Minister, British
                    Minister and myself.<anchor n="75" xml:id="d219-f1"/> Text is substantially same
                    as that given in Department’s 315, November 10 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >9</hi>].<anchor n="76" xml:id="d219-f2"/> British Minister and I
                    simultaneously presented two notes to Foreign Office. First informed Iranian
                    Government that British and American Governments are jointly arranging to bring
                    into Iran 25,000 tons wheat. Second stated that if Soviet Government wishes to
                    participate in declaration a revised text will be signed to replace present one.
                    British Minister also presented note declaring that declaration in no way
                    diminishes British obligations under Tripartite Post [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Pact</hi>] of January 29, 1942. Original of declaration and copies of notes
                    being forwarded airmail. Declaration will be published at once in Tehran and
                    London.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dreyfus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
